# Rendered per run. The filter is default-deny: a domain absent from the
# allowlist is refused, so a skill's outbound attempt is a refusal to observe
# rather than a connection to discover afterwards.
User nobody
Group nogroup
Port 8888
Listen 0.0.0.0
Timeout 600
LogLevel Warning
MaxClients 32
Filter "/etc/tinyproxy/filter"
FilterDefaultDeny Yes
# The filter entries are extended regexps (they use "(", ")" and "|" for
# grouping and alternation); under basic regex those are literal characters
# and every anchored entry would match nothing, which combined with
# FilterDefaultDeny Yes is a silent total egress block, not a working allowlist.
FilterExtended On
FilterCaseSensitive Off
ConnectPort 443
